    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d736">

                <pb facs="0652" n="643" xml:id="pg643"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6612: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Leopoldville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mallon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leopoldville</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-11-11T22:00:00+01:00">November 11,
                            1940—10 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 12—10:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram dated October 31. Libreville taken by De Gaulle forces
                    November 10 by air and sea attack. General Tetu taken prisoner. De Gaulle
                    reports very little bloodshed, insists that no British forces took part, sees
                    possibility of retaliatory measures against Pointe-Noire and Fort Lamy by Dakar
                    troops.</p>
                <p>The Governor General of the Belgian Congo gave a very strong pro-British pro-De
                    Gaulle Armistice Day address.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mallon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
